<p>
 <br>
</p>
<h1 id=3D"MultiFirmUseCases-ExpectedUserSetupStandards">Expected User Setup=
 Standards</h1>
<p>This section outlines the way in which users&nbsp;<strong>should</strong=
> be setup in the in scope systems to obtain access to their parent firm an=
d/or sub-advisor RR codes/ranges</p>
<h3 id=3D"MultiFirmUseCases-R2">R2</h3>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"8e85dff3-978c-4822-9e05-8c3e6ce91a1b"><span>Parent/Child =
users have one user ID per FirmID</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"982969d8-c284-41db-b2ae-60ee8c2c1184"><span>Sub-advisors =
users setup under their "primary" firm</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c1f62f87-fff1-4a30-8912-05b2602035aa"><span>Only primary =
firm RR codes should be present in the RR code field</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"be12528e-e798-433d-8f45-8da45778f5a5"><span>Only sub-advi=
sor firm RR codes should be present in the sub-advisor RR code field</span>=
</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0527d58f-8653-4ca3-b168-09192d1b1cf4"><span>RR ranges can=
not be specified</span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"MultiFirmUseCases-SecureZone">Secure Zone</h3>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"4c59357a-563e-4033-84ff-e68a5d0d2aa6"><span>Users are set=
up under B#'s (which can be shared or standalone)</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f539e4ce-2799-4b71-8216-97273515e66b"><span>Users are ass=
ociated to 1 or many B#'s, giving them access to</span><span> all the firms=
 they need (parent/child and sub-advisor)</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e7710ebe-54eb-4b8e-ab8b-4c20fca6fab2">Within the associat=
ed B#'s the user can have access to ALL or some of the RR codes of a partic=
ular B#.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"dab7a957-0d85-4a27-bed0-1971facda7a0">There is no FirmID =
connection to the user</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"9eab09ae-4a0e-4f81-ad46-0a143fac7e95"><span>RR ranges can=
not be specified. In the case of access to the full set of RR codes, it is =
indicated as ALL.</span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"MultiFirmUseCases-NetRep">NetRep</h3>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c6807b23-7a65-4643-a47c-754f325e15fb">User must be setup =
in one of the 3 instances of NetRep, but can be setup in multiple&nbsp;
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"639e13d3-753b-4aa2-a6ae-547126fb0e69">HSW - Nextrep IA =
(IAVM)</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"a96f96f4-411a-48fa-8771-9aa39b9a18e7">NPM - NetRep PM</=
li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"40741680-1456-428d-bb77-90f69b6bd698">NBC - NetRep 2.0<=
/li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0db2fcaa-e2dd-45e4-8519-dc25f0ba74e1">User is granted to =
RR codes or Ranges (using the first 2 digits of the RR code)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"67836639-9070-4421-9a77-41c49f03946d">Users obtain access=
 to all the firms they need based on the assigned RR codes or ranges.&nbsp;=
</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"bda5e2ab-21b4-4355-bd63-9af49850ce32">There is no associa=
tion to a B# or FirmID</li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"MultiFirmUseCases-Edgecases">Edge cases</h1>
