<hr>
<h2 id=3D"MultiFirmUseCases-Sub-advisor">Sub-advisor</h2>
<p><span>Based on the meeting on March 26th, 2026 with Aman G. from the Cli=
ent Implementation team, the following outlines how Sub-advisor relationshi=
ps are currently appeared across NetRep, R2 and CX using the sample Firm ID=
 ICPMB_HIVFG. (SZ was included in the initial analysis but found to have mi=
nimal connection/relevance to this workflow.)=20
  <br>=20
  <br></span></p>
<ul>
 <li><span>HIGHVIEW ASSET MGMT LTD.&nbsp; (ICPMB_HIVFG)&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>
  <ul>
   <li><span>Initially assigned 5 RR codes A48F, A48G, A48H, A48I, A48J in =
September 2025.=20
     <br></span></li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"179d6ff1-e0db-4cc4-81a7-196aaecf2df4"><span><span style=
=3D"color:#c9372c;">A48G, A48H, A48I</span> - 3 of these 5 codes are alloca=
ted for Sub-Advisor use.</span></li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li><span>Key Findings</span>
  <ol>
   <li data-uuid=3D"d195980a-780a-4e0f-9cdf-b1260c9d6333"><span>New Account=
 Creation Under Target Firm -&nbsp;ICPMB_HIVFG=20
     <br></span>
    <p>When an external user acts as a sub-advisor for <strong>ICPMB_HIVFG<=
/strong>, user IDs are created directly under the <strong>ICPMB_HIVFG</stro=
ng> Firm ID across <strong>NetRep, CX, and R2</strong>.
     <br>
     <br></p></li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"ed8f155f-8036-491e-b3e5-71bc6c8ffec4">
    <p>In this scenario, a new user ID is created specifically for sub-advi=
sing purposes, and it is <em>not</em> common practice to add sub-advisor RR=
 codes to an existing user ID.</p>
    <p>However, in <strong>R2</strong>, there are instances where existing =
user IDs have sub-advisor RR codes populated in the <strong>Sub_Advisor_Cod=
e</strong> column.</p>
    <span>=20
     <br>=20
     <strong>R2</strong>=20
     <br>=20
    </span>
